{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765501,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"Free Fire MAX","festival_id":520986,"organization_id":825345,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-11-15T23:59:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/free-fire-max-scaler-school-of-technology-bengaluru-karnataka-1765501","region":"hybrid","details":"<p><strong>Tournament Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Game: Free Fire MAX<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Format: Battle Royale (BR)<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Tournament Stages: Online Qualifiers, Offline Semifinals, and Offline Grand Finals<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Venue: Scaler School of Technology (SST) (All offline stages)<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Team Composition: 4 Starting Players + 1 Optional Substitute (Roster size up to 5 players)<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Player and Team Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Roster Requirements: Each registered squad must have 4 starters and at most 1 substitute. Rosters lock immediately upon the official start of each match.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Verification: Player UIDs, in-game nicknames, account levels, and real identities are subject to strict administrative audit. Unverified accounts will be disqualified.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Roster Restrictions: Players may not compete on more than one roster. Mid-match substitutions are strictly prohibited; substitutes may only enter the lineup between matches.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Tournament Stage Progression:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The progression pathway transitions initial squads through online rounds and offline semifinals into a 12-team Grand Final.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><strong>Stage Breakdown:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Online Qualifiers: Divided into some groups of 12or 11 teams each. Each group plays 3 Battle Royale matches. The top 3 teams from each group plus the best 4th-place finisher across all 7 groups advance to the Semifinals (total 22 teams).<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Offline Semifinals: Divided into groups of 12 or 11 teams each at the SST venue. Each group plays 3 Battle Royale matches. The top 6 teams from each group qualify directly for the Grand Finals (total 12 teams).<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Offline Grand Finals (12 Finalists): A single lobby of 12 teams playing 5 Battle Royale matches. Cumulative points across all matches determine the Champion, Runner-up, and Second Runner-up.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Official Scoring System:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Scores are reset to zero at the start of each stage. Stage scores are calculated as the sum of Placement Points and Kill Points across all matches in that stage.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Kill Points:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">+1 Point for every confirmed kill.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Placement Points Table<\/span><\/h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"3\">&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table style=\"width: 42.4474%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td styl